.TH MAKED 1 "October 2026" "maked 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
maked \- High-Performance POSIX/GNU-Compatible Build Utility Certified with Lean 4 Formal Semantics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B maked
[\fB\-B\fR]
[\fB\-b\fR]
[\fB\-C\fR \fIdir\fR]
[\fB\-e\fR]
[\fB\-f\fR \fIfile\fR]
[\fB\-h\fR]
[\fB\-\-hash\fR]
[\fB\-i\fR]
[\fB\-j\fR [\fIN\fR]]
[\fB\-k\fR]
[\fB\-m\fR]
[\fB\-n\fR]
[\fB\-p\fR]
[\fB\-\-profile\fR]
[\fB\-q\fR]
[\fB\-s\fR]
[\fB\-t\fR]
[\fB\-v\fR]
[\fIVAR\fR=\fIVALUE\fR ...]
[\fItarget\fR ...]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B maked
is a high-performance, memory-safe, dependency-directed build utility designed as a modern
re-implementation of the classic Make build system. It adheres strictly to the
.B IEEE Std 1003.1 (POSIX)
specification, supports major
.B GNU Make
extensions (including core built-in text manipulation functions, pattern rules, and VPATH search),
and features certified correctness proofs verified in the
.B Lean 4
theorem prover.

Additionally,
.B maked
supports an optional cryptographic content hashing mode (\fB\-\-hash\fR) powered by a zero-dependency
FIPS 180-4 compliant SHA-256 digest engine, tracking file contents and recipe changes in a local
cache database (\fB.maked.db\fR) to achieve build hermeticity and resistance against filesystem timestamp tampering.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-B ", " \-\-always\-make
Unconditionally build all targets regardless of modification timestamps or hash records.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-m
POSIX compatibility flags; ignored with no effect.
.TP
.BI \-C " dir"
Change working directory to \fIdir\fR before parsing makefiles or executing target recipes.
.TP
.BI \-e ", " \-\-environment\-overrides
Give environment variables precedence over macro definitions inside makefiles.
Command-line macro assignments (\fIVAR=VAL\fR) retain strict top priority.
.TP
.BI \-f " file"
Use \fIfile\fR as the makefile. If omitted,
.B maked
searches for \fBMakefile\fR and \fBmakefile\fR in the current working directory.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage summary and options, then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-hash
Enable cryptographic SHA-256 content hashing. Targets and prerequisites are evaluated based on
content digests and recipe command strings rather than filesystem modification timestamps.
Build records are cached in \fB.maked.db\fR.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-ignore\-errors
Ignore non-zero return codes from all recipe commands.
.TP
.BI \-j " [N]"
Execute recipes concurrently using \fIN\fR worker threads. If \fIN\fR is omitted, the concurrency
level defaults to the system's available hardware thread count.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-keep\-going
Continue processing independent branches of the dependency DAG even after encountering an error.
.TP
.BI \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print recipe commands that would be executed without actually executing them.
.TP
.BI \-p ", " \-\-print\-data\-base
Print the complete internal database of variables, pattern rules, and explicit rules.
.TP
.B \-\-profile
Display granular execution telemetry upon completion, including targets evaluated, rebuilt,
up to date, commands dispatched, and elapsed wall-clock time.
.TP
.BI \-q ", " \-\-question
Question mode: do not run any recipes. Return exit code 0 if all requested goals are up to date,
or 1 if any target requires rebuilding.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-silent ", " \-\-quiet
Do not echo recipe commands before executing them.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-touch
Touch targets (updating their filesystem timestamp to current time or creating empty files)
instead of executing recipe commands.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version, standards compliance information, and formal verification credentials, then exit.

.TP
.BI \-\-worker\-listen= ADDR
Run as a remote build worker on \fIADDR\fR. Requires a shared token in the file
named by \fBMAKED_WORKER_TOKEN_FILE\fR or in \fBMAKED_WORKER_TOKEN\fR (at least 16 bytes).
Non-loopback addresses are refused unless \fB\-\-worker\-allow\-remote\fR is given.
Requests and responses are authenticated with HMAC-SHA256 but not encrypted.
.TP
.B \-\-worker\-allow\-remote
Allow \fB\-\-worker\-listen\fR to accept connections from other hosts.
.TP
.BI \-\-remote\-workers= ADDR[,ADDR...]
Send recipes to remote workers, round-robin, using the same token. A target falls back
to a local build when a worker is unreachable or fails.
.SH AUTOMATIC VARIABLES
The following POSIX automatic variables are dynamically populated in recipe command scopes:
.TP
.B $@
The name of the target currently being made.
.TP
.B $<
The name of the first prerequisite in the rule.
.TP
.B $^
The names of all prerequisites in the rule, separated by spaces, with duplicate entries removed.
.TP
.B $*
The stem of the target (target filename stripped of its suffix or pattern match).
.TP
.B $$
A literal dollar sign character.

.SH BUILT-IN FUNCTIONS
.B maked
implements the complete GNU Make standard function library:
.TP
.B $(wildcard \fIpattern ...\fR)
Expands to a space-separated list of existing files matching the glob pattern(s).
.TP
.B $(patsubst \fIpattern\fR,\fIreplacement\fR,\fItext\fR)
Replaces words matching \fIpattern\fR with \fIreplacement\fR, preserving the matched stem (%).
.TP
.B $(subst \fIfrom\fR,\fIto\fR,\fItext\fR)
Replaces every occurrence of substring \fIfrom\fR with \fIto\fR in \fItext\fR.
.TP
.B $(filter \fIpattern ...\fR,\fItext\fR)
Returns words in \fItext\fR that match any of the given patterns.
.TP
.B $(filter-out \fIpattern ...\fR,\fItext\fR)
Returns words in \fItext\fR that do not match any of the given patterns.
.TP
.B $(dir \fInames ...\fR)
Extracts the directory component of each file name.
.TP
.B $(notdir \fInames ...\fR)
Extracts the non-directory file name component of each name.
.TP
.B $(suffix \fInames ...\fR)
Extracts the suffix (extension including dot) of each file name.
.TP
.B $(basename \fInames ...\fR)
Extracts the basename (file name without suffix) of each file name.
.TP
.B $(addprefix \fIprefix\fR,\fInames ...\fR)
Prepends \fIprefix\fR to each word.
.TP
.B $(addsuffix \fIsuffix\fR,\fInames ...\fR)
Appends \fIsuffix\fR to each word.
.TP
.B $(join \fIlist1\fR,\fIlist2\fR)
Joins words in \fIlist1\fR and \fIlist2\fR pairwise.
.TP
.B $(word \fIn\fR,\fItext\fR)
Returns the 1-indexed \fIn\fR-th word of \fItext\fR.
.TP
.B $(words \fItext\fR)
Returns the number of whitespace-separated words in \fItext\fR.
.TP
.B $(firstword \fInames ...\fR)
Returns the first word of \fInames\fR.
.TP
.B $(lastword \fInames ...\fR)
Returns the last word of \fInames\fR.
.TP
.B $(sort \fIlist\fR)
Sorts words lexicographically and removes duplicates.
.TP
.B $(strip \fIstring\fR)
Strips leading and trailing whitespace and collapses internal whitespace runs into single spaces.
.TP
.B $(shell \fIcommand\fR)
Executes \fIcommand\fR in a subshell, replacing newlines with spaces and returning standard output.
.TP
.B $(if \fIcondition\fR,\fIthen-part\fR[,\fIelse-part\fR])
Conditionally evaluates and expands arguments.
.TP
.B $(or \fIc1\fR[,\fIc2 ...\fR])
Returns the first non-empty expansion.
.TP
.B $(and \fIc1\fR[,\fIc2 ...\fR])
Returns the last expansion if all are non-empty; otherwise expands to empty.

.SH VPATH SEARCH
When a target or prerequisite does not exist in the current working directory,
.B maked
searches directory search paths specified via:
.IP 1.
The \fBvpath\fR directive: \fBvpath\fR \fIpattern\fR \fIdirectories ...\fR
.IP 2.
The \fBVPATH\fR environment or makefile variable (colon- or space-separated list of paths).
.PP
When found, the prerequisite path is updated so automatic variables ($<, $^) reflect the actual location.

.SH FORMAL VERIFICATION
The operational semantics of
.B maked
are formally specified and mechanically certified in
.B Lean 4
(\fIlean_make/LeanMake/Theorems.lean\fR).
Verified theorems include:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBexecuteRule_clock_monotonic\fR: Build clock advances monotonically.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBphony_always_rebuilds\fR: Phony rules with commands unconditionally rebuild.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBmissing_always_rebuilds\fR: Missing targets unconditionally trigger recipe execution.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBupToDate_needs_no_rebuild\fR: Fresh target states require zero rebuilds.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcycle_trace_head\fR: Graph cycle detector correctly pinpoints recursion culprits.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBrebuild_strictly_fresher_than_dep\fR: Target timestamp strictly exceeds all prerequisite timestamps upon rebuild.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBexecuteRule_upToDate_idempotent\fR: Certified single-step and inductive DAG idempotency under POSIX freshness.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful completion; or in question mode (\fB\-q\fR), all targets are up to date.
.TP
.B 1
A recipe command exited with an error; or in question mode (\fB\-q\fR), one or more targets require rebuilding.
.TP
.B 2
A makefile syntax error, circular dependency cycle, or fatal invocation error occurred.

.SH CONFORMANCE
.B maked
strictly complies with:
.IP \(bu 2
.B IEEE Std 1003.1-2017 (POSIX.1)
Make utility specification.
.IP \(bu 2
.B GNU Make 4.4+
macro, function, and pattern rule extensions.
.IP \(bu 2
.B FIPS 180-4
Secure Hash Standard (SHA-256).

